# Flush Borders

The website and app use flush panels: rows, columns and sections are separated by 1px `border-secondary-800` lines, not by gaps or cards. Every UI change must end with **exactly one line** between two blocks: never a missing line, never two lines stacked.

## Check before finishing

Look at (or screenshot) every edited panel and check these spots:

- **Shorter column in a grid**: when two or more columns sit side by side, the shorter one must still close with a line under its last row
- **Last row of a list or panel**: its bottom line must not stack on the parent's bottom border
- **Last block on the page**: the site footer has its own `border-t`; the block above it must not add a `border-b`
- **Stacked on mobile**: a `divide-y` between columns that already close with their own line gives a double line below `lg`
- **Clipped grids**: `overflow-hidden` + negative margins can hide a bottom line you still need

## Patterns

- **Columns of rows**: give each row/cell `border-b` (not `divide-y`) and pull the list `-mb-px` so its last line lands on the parent's closing border
- **Grid cells**: cells draw `border-r border-b`; the wrapper is `-mb-px overflow-hidden` and the grid `-mr-px` (see `packages/ui/src/docs/docs-ref-grid.svelte`)
- **Two-column layouts**: `lg:divide-x` only; each column's children close themselves (`[&>*]:border-b`) and the grid is `-mb-px` (see `docs-layout.svelte`)

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — shorter column has no closing line; on mobile divide-y doubles the line -->
<div class="grid divide-y lg:grid-cols-2 lg:divide-x lg:divide-y-0">
	<ul class="divide-y">…</ul>
	<ul class="divide-y">…</ul>
</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — every row closes itself; the list overlaps the panel's closing line -->
<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:divide-x">
	<ul class="-mb-px">
		<li class="border-secondary-800 border-b">…</li>
	</ul>
	<ul class="-mb-px">
		<li class="border-secondary-800 border-b">…</li>
	</ul>
</div>
```

## Do not

- Finish a layout change without checking the bottom of every column and the line above the footer
- Add `border-b` to the last block before the footer
- Use `divide-y` on a grid whose columns stack on mobile and already end with a line
